  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759317,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Supervision 110-in-1: A Retro Gaming Bonanza (with a Catch!)\n\nThe Supervision 110-in-1 is a legendary multicart for the Nintendo Entertainment System (NES), released in the early 1990s. It promises a staggering 93 games on a single cartridge, offering an incredible variety of experiences – from action and adventure to puzzle and sports titles. While the sheer volume is enticing, be warned: the current ROM dump is notoriously flawed, leading to glitches and unplayable games.\n\nExpect a mix of officially licensed titles, unlicensed games, and even some homebrew creations. Many are simplified or shortened versions of popular games, while others are entirely unique. Gameplay varies wildly across the collection. You might find yourself battling hordes of enemies in a side-scrolling action game, solving intricate puzzles, or competing in fast-paced sports challenges. \n\nDespite the technical issues, the Supervision 110-in-1 remains a fascinating artifact of the NES era, a testament to the ingenuity (and sometimes questionable practices) of unlicensed game development. It's a nostalgic trip for retro enthusiasts, but approach with the understanding that not every game will be a perfect experience."
    },
